-- Float literal regression (plan 0.71 F7). Expected exit code 3
--
-- The literal is USED — passed to `emitF` — so this asks nothing about dead
-- code elimination. The SigOp's runtime is a nop; the observable is that the
-- process REACHES its exit code instead of trapping.
--
-- This is the test that would have caught D109 on the day float literals
-- landed: under the pre-0.66 x86-32 lowering a float constant compiled to
-- `ud2`, so on that target this program died instead of exiting 3. It runs
-- on x86-64, x86-32 and riscv64, and 0.125 is exact at every width — four
-- significand bits suffice, so it stays valid on a narrower target too.

import I.Linux.Syscalls as S
import I.Test.Emit as T

main : IO Unit
main = let _ = emitF@T 0.125 in exit@S 3
